-- Sharing metadata.  Read by tooling and the manager detail pane; never by the
-- loader's merge.
return {
  summary = "FireRed/LeafGreen port of the Gen 1/2 Dialogue Portraits mod: "
    .. "shows a portrait of whoever is talking, next to the dialogue box.",
  author = "Almdar",
  tags = { "ui", "visual", "gen3", "firered", "leafgreen", "portraits" },
  differences = {
    added = {
      "INSET (the default): a 32px portrait fills the slot's own four columns "
        .. "edge to edge -- no margin between the picture and the frame it sits "
        .. "in -- with one more column kept clear of the words, and the text "
        .. "moves along.  BOTH sides reserve the same five columns, so SIDE does "
        .. "not change how much text there is: 168px of the box's 208 either "
        .. "way.  It used to reserve four columns on the left and five on the "
        .. "right, which made the same layout a different width on each side.  "
        .. "The 32px is the box's own four-row content rect, and the crop that "
        .. "fills it, so nothing is stretched and no pixel doubles.  The slot "
        .. "did not move: it has been 32px since 1.8.3, and the reserve is still "
        .. "five columns.  1.6.0 made the portrait 38px, which is taller than "
        .. "that rect, so the only way to place it was to clamp it against the "
        .. "visible box's top border rather than to centre it in the rect it "
        .. "occupies; 1.8.x drew a 30px portrait in the 32px slot, which left a "
        .. "one-pixel band of box on every side.",
      "FRAMED: the game's own standard menu window -- the same Chrome.stdFrame "
        .. "the start menu's box and the OPTION page's body are drawn with, so it "
        .. "is drawn in the player's own OPTION -> FRAME choice -- six tiles "
        .. "(48px) square, with a whole tile (8px) of border on every side around "
        .. "a 32px content rect.  The border is drawn from 8x8 tiles and only "
        .. "lines up on the tile grid, so the window is ONE size for everybody and "
        .. "the ART is what varies: it is fitted into the content at the largest "
        .. "whole number of times its own crop that fits -- the default 32px face "
        .. "at 1:1 filling the content exactly, a 16px crop at 2x also filling "
        .. "it, a 12px one at 2x with four pixels of content either side -- and "
        .. "never resampled to an arbitrary fit.  Because the window is a "
        .. "constant the text width is a constant again -- 152px for every "
        .. "speaker in this layout, which reverses 1.8.0's per-speaker width -- "
        .. "and the run the box gives up is a constant 7 columns.  The panel is "
        .. "CENTRED in the columns the box gave up, so its outer edge keeps "
        .. "EDGE_PAD -- 4 game px -- from the play area's own edge and its inner "
        .. "edge the same 4px from the box's VISIBLE edge: it touches neither "
        .. "the box nor the screen, and the gap the player sees is the constant "
        .. "itself rather than the run's rounding.  The distance from the "
        .. "portrait to the nearest letter is that 4px plus the box's own 16px "
        .. "border: 20px, on both sides.  It used to send the whole slack to "
        .. "the outer side -- which on the default crop meant no slack at all, "
        .. "so the panel sat flush against the box AND touched the edge of the "
        .. "play area, which on a phone IS the edge of the screen.  1.4.0 "
        .. "stretched the art into a fixed "
        .. "six-tile panel (a 30px face drawn at 46px), 1.6.0 kept that panel and "
        .. "stretched the art into a 46px window inside it, and 1.8.0 sized the "
        .. "panel to the art and painted a one-pixel black outline where a border "
        .. "should be; this release takes the fixed size back, but as a real "
        .. "window rather than a stretch, and the ring around the art is the "
        .. "game's own tile-drawn border instead of a hairline.",
      "MARGIN: the same window moved clear of the box, painted out in the "
        .. "letterbox through render.hud, on the side SIDE asks for, and "
        .. "costing the text nothing.  It draws the SAME window FRAMED does -- "
        .. "the game's own 48px menu frame around a content rect the art is "
        .. "centred in at a whole-number zoom, scaled by the window's own unit -- "
        .. "so a small crop is enlarged by a whole number instead of being "
        .. "stretched to fill the window.  With no letterbox to use it stands "
        .. "above the box instead, keeping MARGIN_BOX_GAP -- 2 game px -- clear "
        .. "of the box's top and MARGIN_PAD -- 4 game px -- in from the edge of "
        .. "the play area.  Those are two different margins and 1.9.3 is where "
        .. "they stopped sharing one constant: the distance the panel keeps from "
        .. "the BOX is not the distance it keeps from the SCREEN.  It used to be "
        .. "2 game px above the box and flush with the play area's "
        .. "own edge, which on a phone IS the edge of the screen.  "
        .. "It is measured against the rect the frame was actually DRAWN at, "
        .. "asked of the renderer THROUGH require, rather than the one render.hud "
        .. "reports -- a mod does not run against _G, and the package in its "
        .. "sandbox is LegacyCompat's packageShim, a decoy whose loaded is a "
        .. "fresh empty table, so 1.8.0's package.loaded lookup answered nil and "
        .. "its fix never ran in the game while every test passed.  The "
        .. "renderer's rect is the one the frame is drawn from: the "
        .. "payload comes from Display.fit (48% of the safe area, scale from the "
        .. "width alone) while the frame is drawn from the touch skin's own "
        .. "cutout (a fraction of the window, scale from both axes), and the two "
        .. "disagree by up to 41 game px on a phone -- 0 on a desktop, where no "
        .. "skin is selected, which is why it never showed there.  A panel "
        .. "placed against the reported box sat anywhere from 33 game px inside "
        .. "the real box to 46 above it.  The payload is still used when there "
        .. "is no renderer to ask, and the panel is placed in the WINDOW's own "
        .. "units: scale is integer FRAMEBUFFER pixels per game pixel while "
        .. "gameX and gameWidth are window units, and the two differ by the "
        .. "display's pixel ratio -- 1 on a desktop, 2 or 3 on a phone, because "
        .. "conf.lua sets highdpi on mobile only.",
      "SIDE = AUTO, which reads the player's own facing -- you turn left to "
        .. "talk to somebody on your left, so that is the side their face "
        .. "belongs on.  Facing up or down says nothing either way and keeps "
        .. "the traditional LEFT.",
      "Two mod options: PORTRAIT (INSET / FRAMED / MARGIN / OFF) and SIDE "
        .. "(AUTO / LEFT / RIGHT), reached through a DIALOGUE PORTRAITS group "
        .. "inside FireRed's own OPTION menu.",
      "The cart's own GRAPHICS ID decides who an NPC is, before their class "
        .. "does.  The engine's host sprite vocabulary is not FRLG's "
        .. "OBJ_EVENT_GFX_*: several graphics collapse onto one sprite (the "
        .. "Man, the Balding Man and the Hiker are all SPRITE_POKEFAN_M), two "
        .. "are mapped onto a sprite that names a DIFFERENT person (a Camper "
        .. "onto SPRITE_YOUNGSTER, a Picnicker onto SPRITE_LASS), and every "
        .. "graphic the host table does not list falls back to "
        .. "SPRITE_YOUNGSTER -- so a Hiker wore the PokeFan's face, so did a "
        .. "Man and a Balding Man (and that picture is a BOY's), and every "
        .. "Bug Catcher, Rocket, Swimmer, Tuber, Channeler and gym leader wore "
        .. "a boy's.  The object carries its real graphics id, and a graphic is "
        .. "one person or one uniform while a class can cover eight gym "
        .. "leaders or both sexes of one kind, so it is consulted FIRST and "
        .. "answers with an exact front picture, a name resolved through the "
        .. "trainer pack, or -- for the five graphics the cart never drew a "
        .. "battle bust of -- with no portrait at all.  It is also what "
        .. "separates a male Cooltrainer from a female one, and a male Tuber "
        .. "from a female one: each pair shares a sprite and a class, so both "
        .. "resolved through the class name to whichever id it reached first, "
        .. "and each was wearing the other's face.  A graphic the host has no "
        .. "mapping for is not answered by the host's fallback either: it "
        .. "closes the sprite route, because the sprite the object carries is "
        .. "then the host's own guess rather than a fact about the person.",
      "Pokemon standing in the world have faces.  FRLG places Pokemon as map "
        .. "objects and names each one with its own OBJ_EVENT_GFX_* id -- 109 "
        .. "SNORLAX through 150 DEOXYS_N -- and every one of those ids sits "
        .. "above the 92 the host sprite table stops at, so all of them arrived "
        .. "as its SPRITE_YOUNGSTER fallback.  That cost the species twice over: "
        .. "the sprite route reads a species off the SPRITE id and a Youngster "
        .. "is not one, and the same fallback CLOSED the sprite route, because a "
        .. "boy's face on a Spearow is the wrong-portrait bug that rule exists "
        .. "to prevent.  So every Pokemon in the game drew nothing at all -- the "
        .. "reported 'some Pokemon, such as Spearow, do not display a portrait "
        .. "at all'.  The cart's own graphics id is the fact left over and it "
        .. "names the species outright.  32 of the 42 ids are actually placed "
        .. "somewhere in the game, measured with .probe/dp3_nonpeople_sweep.lua "
        .. "rather than assumed; the whole range is mapped because the mapping "
        .. "is exact for every id and OBJ_EVENT_GFX_VAR_* can place any of them "
        .. "at runtime.",
      "Ordinary NPCs have faces.  A map object only carries a trainer CLASS "
        .. "when it is a battle object (objects.lua sets trainerType 0 for "
        .. "everybody else), so on Gen 3 the people the player actually walks "
        .. "up to -- the Lass by the fence, the Hiker on the mountain, the "
        .. "Sailor in the harbour -- are named only by their SPRITE_* id.  "
        .. "Those sprites are mapped to the class whose battle art is the same "
        .. "kind of person, and the graphics id above corrects the cases where "
        .. "that mapping is lossy; what neither route can place gets no "
        .. "portrait rather than a wrong one.",
      "The rival has a face.  His dialogue is the one place in the cart that "
        .. "does not name its speaker: it carries the FD 06 placeholder where "
        .. "the name belongs and the engine expands it to whatever the player "
        .. "typed, so no trainer pack can place it and he is recognised instead "
        .. "by the name on the save.  He is also why a name the mod cannot place "
        .. "no longer discards the object the press resolved -- the object rides "
        .. "alongside the name, and a name the pack DOES know still wins "
        .. "outright, so a script handing off between two characters is "
        .. "unaffected.",
      "A trainer who challenges you has a face.  Their dialogue does not begin "
        .. "with an A press at all: a line-of-sight trainer sees the player and "
        .. "the engine starts their script from a step "
        .. "(src/core/game3/trainer_sight.lua, TrainerSight.engage), which "
        .. "raises no world.talk -- so the press record stayed empty, the "
        .. "resolver had nothing to answer with, and the 'wants to battle' box "
        .. "came out bare.  The engine names the object for exactly this case: "
        .. "engage() emits world.trainer_engaged with the trainer's own event "
        .. "object, and recording that is the same act as recording a press.  "
        .. "Every existing way of ending a conversation drops it again, and the "
        .. "payload's class is only a fallback for an object whose own "
        .. "trainerType has not been stamped yet -- kept in a shallow copy "
        .. "rather than written onto the engine's object, because a mod must "
        .. "not scribble on the world.",
    },
    changed = {
      "The dialogue box gains a portrait, drawn inside the 240x160 game frame "
        .. "for INSET and FRAMED, or over the finished composite for MARGIN.",
      "WHICH portrait belongs to a trainer is now answered the way the cart "
        .. "answers it.  The overworld sprite never decides it -- a sprite is a "
        .. "uniform, and uniforms are shared.  OBJ_EVENT_GFX_ROCKER, the "
        .. "yellow-haired figure, is worn by 28 trainer objects: 18 Bird "
        .. "Keepers, 9 Jugglers and exactly one Rocker, and those three have "
        .. "three different battle pictures.  Sixteen of the 34 graphics a "
        .. "trainer can wear are shared that way by two or more classes whose "
        .. "pictures differ, so no value per sprite can be right for them.  So "
        .. "the rule is two rules: a TRAINER gets his own picture, by id, "
        .. "through the script route above -- all 432 trainer objects in the "
        .. "cart resolve to their id's own front pic, and 0 do not -- and a "
        .. "NON-TRAINER, who has no trainer data at all, gets ONE consistent "
        .. "picture per graphic, because his sprite is the only fact about him "
        .. "there is.",
      "The text's own name no longer overrules a graphic that has already "
        .. "DECLINED.  That is the reported 'fat man Eric in Fuchsia City, who "
        .. "incorrectly has a Scientist portrait': the fat man on Fuchsia "
        .. "City's first object opens 'ERIK: Where's SARA? I said I'd meet her "
        .. "here.', and ERIK IS a real trainer -- id 177, a SUPER NERD whose "
        .. "picture 89 is a man in a white lab coat -- but the fat man is not "
        .. "him and is not a trainer at all.  He wears gfx 27, and GFX_ART says "
        .. "of that graphic, deliberately, that the cart drew no battle bust of "
        .. "this person; a token in a dialogue box cannot make a picture exist. "
        .. "The guard is narrow on purpose and that is measured: sweeping every "
        .. "line of every object in the cart -- 1648 objects, 52 that name "
        .. "someone -- finds 4 non-trainers whose name resolves to a trainer's "
        .. "picture, and 2 of those ARE the trainer they name (LORELEI and "
        .. "SELPHY, who keep their faces).  The same sweep finds 0 trainers "
        .. "whose name route disagrees with their own id and 0 objects where "
        .. "the name disagrees with the graphic it rides on, which is why the "
        .. "name route is still AHEAD of the graphic route rather than deleted "
        .. "-- a script handing off between two characters box by box still "
        .. "comes out right.",
      "Sweeping for that shape rather than waiting for it to be reported found "
        .. "a second instance: DAISY OAK, in the rival's house, whose box opens "
        .. "'DAISY: Hi, PLAYER!'.  The pack has a DAISY -- trainer 526, a "
        .. "PAINTER on Five Island, whose overworld sprite is OBJ_EVENT_GFX_LASS "
        .. "-- and Daisy Oak is the rival's sister, in OBJ_EVENT_GFX_DAISY, and "
        .. "the cart drew no bust of her: the front-pic list is 148 class "
        .. "pictures plus Oak, Red, Leaf, Brendan and May.  She was wearing a "
        .. "Painter's face.  She declines now.",
      "Two graphics the host names after a kind that is only a MINORITY of "
        .. "their wearers now answer with the person the art actually is.  "
        .. "OBJ_EVENT_GFX_ROCKER (26) is the yellow-haired figure and its art is "
        .. "picture 104's -- yellow hair, red shirt, blue overalls -- while "
        .. "picture 101, the Rocker, is a blue-haired punk in an orange jacket; "
        .. "18 Bird Keepers and 9 Jugglers wear the graphic against the one "
        .. "Rocker, so the 8 non-trainers on it now get the Bird Keeper (the 28 "
        .. "trainers get their own ids).  OBJ_EVENT_GFX_LITTLE_GIRL (17) is the "
        .. "red-haired little girl and she is one of the TWINS, not a Lass: the "
        .. "8 Twins get picture 127 by id and the 18 ordinary girls on the "
        .. "graphic get it from the table, where they wore the Lass's 84 before.",
      "The BALDING MAN is not a person the cart failed to draw -- it is the "
        .. "cart's own overworld sprite for the ENGINEER, and 1.9.4 measured "
        .. "that rather than assuming it.  Every one of the cart's three "
        .. "Engineer objects wears gfx 30 (Braxton and Baily on Route 11, and "
        .. "the Engineer in Vermilion Gym) and NO other trainer class wears it "
        .. "at all, so picture 93 -- the Engineer in a hard hat with a wrench "
        .. "and a toolbox -- is the cart's bust of this exact person.  The 28 "
        .. "ordinary balding men in the world are the same person the Engineers "
        .. "are, so they stop declining and get 93 too.  That is the reported "
        .. "'Engineer Braxton's incorrect portrait': Braxton's own answer was "
        .. "already right, but the graphic he wears answered nobody.",
      "A picture the cart drew TWO people into is now cut per person.  Five "
        .. "front pictures hold two figures -- 127 Twins, 128 Cool Couple, 129 "
        .. "Young Couple, 130 Crush Kin, 131 Sis and Bro -- and one window "
        .. "cannot be right for both, so art/crops.lua gains a `pairs` table of "
        .. "a rectangle per half and a `pairSide` table from graphics id to "
        .. "half.  The object's own sprite picks the half it stands on, so the "
        .. "Young Couple's woman (gfx 29, BEAUTY) and man (gfx 25, MAN) are cut "
        .. "from opposite ends of the same drawing -- the reported JES and GIA, "
        .. "who no longer wear the same face.  `pairSide` is a table of its own "
        .. "rather than nine gfx:<id> crop overrides because a gfx: crop is "
        .. "applied to whatever picture the speaker resolved to, and gfx 29 is "
        .. "not only the woman in a Young Couple -- it is also every ordinary "
        .. "Beauty, who wears picture 98.",
      "Every window in the crop table -- 50 of them, across the two defaults, "
        .. "ten trainer pictures, 31 species and nine pair halves -- was "
        .. "re-measured on all four edges.  Two were wrong.  The left Twin's "
        .. "window was {0,10,32} and her head runs to column 33 while her "
        .. "sister's begins at 35, so it was cutting two columns off her face; "
        .. "it is {2,10,32} now, the only 32px span holding all of her and none "
        .. "of her sister.  And the right half of picture 130 started at y 2 "
        .. "while her ponytail's red band reaches row 0, so it cut the top of "
        .. "it; it starts at 0 now.  Both are pinned by number in the geometry "
        .. "suite, because a window that fits inside the 64x64 source can still "
        .. "be cutting the face inside it -- the property test passed for the "
        .. "window that cut her.",
      "A trainer's own face is found from the SCRIPT the object runs.  The map "
        .. "event does not carry the trainer class -- the extractor keeps the "
        .. "object's scriptKey and drops trainerType, so that field is 0 for "
        .. "every NPC including the trainers -- and until 1.9.3 the mod guessed "
        .. "the class from the overworld SPRITE, which is shared.  That is the "
        .. "reported 'some NPCs show the wrong portrait': a Super Nerd wore the "
        .. "Scientist's picture 107 instead of 89 (sprite SCIENTIST is 8 Super "
        .. "Nerds and 14 Scientists), the twins wore the Lass's 84 instead of "
        .. "127 (sprite LITTLE_GIRL is 8 Twins), and the old bald man in the "
        .. "blue robe wore the old karate instructor's 34 instead of 97 (sprite "
        .. "OLD_MAN_1 is 6 Gamers and 24 ordinary old men, and 97 IS the cart's "
        .. "own old man).  The mod now ships art/trainer_ids.lua -- 432 script "
        .. "keys, each naming exactly one trainer id, dug out of the "
        .. "trainerbattle opcode at the head of that script for every trainer "
        .. "object in the cart -- and resolves scriptKey -> trainer id -> that "
        .. "trainer's own front picture.  The engine's own route "
        .. "(TrainerSight.getTrainerId) is not used: its script bundle covers "
        .. "island 1's eighteen maps and answers for only 15 of the cart's 432 "
        .. "trainer objects.  The new route runs BEFORE the graphics table, so "
        .. "it also rescues the graphics that table deliberately declines, and "
        .. "it only ever reads -- eo.trainerId is never written back, so the "
        .. "engine's trainer sight and Vs. Seeker are untouched.",
      "The portrait FRAMING is measured portrait by portrait instead of "
        .. "trusting one general crop.  1.9.3 re-measured seven species and one "
        .. "trainer picture, and all eight were the same mistake: the rule "
        .. "centres the creature's own box, and the box was not the face.  Four "
        .. "of them -- Fearow {32,0}->{0,20}, Pidgeot {15,0}->{0,3}, Zapdos "
        .. "{16,0}->{0,6} and Moltres {13,0}->{0,30} -- had a WING in the frame "
        .. "and no face at all, because a bird drawn with its wings spread is "
        .. "mostly wing and its head is at an edge of the sprite; Articuno "
        .. "{17,0}->{1,0} had the eye on the left edge.  Slowbro {15,7}->{4,7} "
        .. "was centred on the Shellder clamped to its tail and cut the muzzle "
        .. "off the left; Nidorino {15,5}->{11,14} framed the ears and cut the "
        .. "muzzle off the bottom; and the Hoenn Bug Catcher (picture 66, which "
        .. "only the CLASS route reaches because the NAME 'BUG CATCHER' means "
        .. "class 58) gets {10,9} so the whole hat is in frame.  Every other "
        .. "species and all 147 trainer pictures were checked the same way -- "
        .. "rendering the window over the whole 64x64 source and looking at the "
        .. "result -- and the ones that were already right were left alone.",
      "A trainer class is EXCHANGED for its picture through the engine's own "
        .. "trainer pack, because Gen 3 keeps the two in different number "
        .. "spaces -- class 81 is RIVAL_EARLY and its picture is 106, class 97 is "
        .. "POKeMON PROF. and its picture is 132 -- and TrainerPic.front "
        .. "indexes the picture table, so a class id handed to it returns "
        .. "somebody else's face.  83 of the 106 classes the cart uses pin "
        .. "exactly one picture; the rest cover several characters (one class "
        .. "covers all eight gym leaders) and resolve to the most common, ties "
        .. "to the lowest id.  A name the dialogue used resolves exactly, which "
        .. "is how the gym leaders get their own faces.",
      "A class NAME the cart lists twice resolves to the class it actually "
        .. "fields trainers under, not to the lowest id.  FRLG carries its whole "
        .. "Hoenn roster first and repeats 31 of those names for its own Kanto "
        .. "classes further down -- LASS is 49 and again 59, FISHERMAN 31 and "
        .. "69, BEAUTY 12 and 73, SAILOR 41 and 60, BLACK BELT 16 and 80, "
        .. "GENTLEMAN 22 and 88 -- and the two are different people with "
        .. "different battle art.  'Lowest id wins' therefore answered the Hoenn "
        .. "class for all 31, which is the reported 'certain NPCs display an "
        .. "incorrect portrait': the girl on Route 3 (a class-59 Lass) wore the "
        .. "Hoenn Lass's picture 65, and the Hoenn Fisherman, Beauty, Sailor, "
        .. "Black Belt and Gentleman were on every pier, towel and deck in "
        .. "Kanto.  The cart's own trainer rows are the evidence, because the "
        .. "class the game fields trainers under is the one with rows -- "
        .. "FISHERMAN is 69 with 15 rows against 31's 1, LASS 59 with 26 "
        .. "against 49's 1, YOUNGSTER 57 with 28 against 29's 1 -- and of the "
        .. "cart's 742 rows, only 53 sit under a name's low-id half.  Ties go "
        .. "to the higher id, which is the one pair that matters and the reason "
        .. "the rival's picture is a constant.",
      "The dialogue box's own geometry -- Chrome.DLG_W and DLG_LEFT -- is "
        .. "changed for the length of one draw and put straight back, so FRAMED "
        .. "is a per-box change with nothing left behind.  The restore happens "
        .. "on the error path too.",
      "The INSET text shift is scoped to the dialogue box's own text by a flag "
        .. "the draw wrapper raises around its call, so no menu string, party "
        .. "label or battle line is ever moved.",
      "INSET reserves the same run on both sides.  It used to reserve the "
        .. "art's own columns on the left and one more on the right -- the extra "
        .. "one being the blinking arrow's -- so the same layout was a different "
        .. "width on each side, and the left-hand words sat one pixel off the "
        .. "art instead of a column clear of it.  Both sides now reserve the "
        .. "same five, so the text is 21 columns either way and SIDE is not a "
        .. "width.",
      "MARGIN is scaled in the window's own units.  render.hud's viewport "
        .. "reports scale as integer FRAMEBUFFER pixels per game pixel "
        .. "(Renderer:fitScale) while gameX and gameWidth are LOVE window "
        .. "units, so gameWidth is NOT Display.W * scale -- the two differ by "
        .. "exactly the display's pixel ratio.  conf.lua sets t.window.highdpi "
        .. "on mobile only, so that ratio is 1 on a desktop and 2 or 3 on a "
        .. "phone; read as window units, scale drew the panel three times too "
        .. "large on a 3x phone and put its top edge about a hundred pixels "
        .. "below the bottom of the game frame.  The scale comes from the "
        .. "renderer's own frame rect now, with the payload's playfield "
        .. "rectangle (gameWidth / Display.W) as the fallback -- which is what "
        .. "the Gen 2 port has always used (unit = vp.gameWidth / 160).",
      "MARGIN is measured against the rect the frame was actually DRAWN at, not "
        .. "the one render.hud reports.  The payload is Game3:_drawHud's "
        .. "Display.fit(w, h): centred in 48% of the SAFE AREA, scale from the "
        .. "WIDTH alone.  The frame is drawn by Renderer:endFrame from "
        .. "Renderer:frameRects(), which fits the picture into Playfield.cutout "
        .. "-- the TOUCH SKIN's viewport, a fraction of the WINDOW -- and takes "
        .. "its scale from BOTH axes.  The two agree only when no skin is "
        .. "selected, so a desktop never showed it; on a phone they differ by up "
        .. "to 41 game px, and a panel placed MARGIN_PAD above the reported box "
        .. "landed anywhere from 33 game px inside the real box to 46 above it "
        .. "(that range measured at the 8 the constant then had; at today's 4 it "
        .. "is 37 inside to 42 above).  "
        .. "MARGIN is the only layout that can be wrong about this, because "
        .. "INSET and FRAMED draw inside the canvas, where the box is wherever "
        .. "Chrome says it is.  frameRect asks the renderer for the UI rect "
        .. "(uox/uoy/uvpw/uvph -- where endFrame blits the canvas the dialogue "
        .. "box is drawn into) rather than the world rect (ox/oy), which is the "
        .. "same numbers only while the UI scale equals fitScale.  The lookup "
        .. "goes through require, NOT package.loaded: a mod's environment is "
        .. "Sandbox.envFor's, whose package is LegacyCompat's packageShim -- a "
        .. "decoy with a fresh empty loaded -- so package.loaded[Renderer] is nil "
        .. "in the game and a real table only in a suite compiled against _G.  "
        .. "1.8.0 used it, so the branch never ran, MARGIN went on measuring the "
        .. "reported rect, and every test still passed; 1.8.1 fixes the lookup "
        .. "and builds the suite's environment the way the loader does.",
      "The engine's word-wrap is told the layout's own text width.  "
        .. "Message.show wraps the box once against ctx.maxWidth, defaulting to "
        .. "a hardcoded 208 -- the vanilla box's own 26 columns -- while "
        .. "Message.drawText clips each line at Chrome.DLG_W * Display.TILE, "
        .. "which follows the geometry.  Vanilla the two agree; every layout "
        .. "here breaks that, and only the clip used to follow, so a line ran "
        .. "on under the portrait instead of breaking where it was drawn.  "
        .. "The caller's opts "
        .. "and ctx are copied rather than mutated -- a script hands the same "
        .. "table to several boxes, and ctx also carries the "
        .. "playerName/rivalName the text placeholders expand through.",
      "FRAMED's panel is anchored to the box the player SEES, and keeps its "
        .. "distance from the play area's edge on its own side: Chrome.DLG_* is "
        .. "the box's content rect, and dialogueFrame draws its border two "
        .. "columns outside that on each side and a row above and below, so the "
        .. "box the player sees is "
        .. "240x48 at (0,112) -- the whole screen width.  Anchored "
        .. "to the content rect instead it sat two columns in from the screen "
        .. "edge and read as part of the box's own border; that was measured by "
        .. ".probe/dp3_chrome_probe.lua rather than read off the constants.  "
        .. "The panel hangs off the box's own VISIBLE edge -- its inner edge "
        .. "lands on it -- and the box gives up the window's run PLUS the "
        .. "clearance, so its outer edge keeps at least EDGE_PAD -- 4 game px -- "
        .. "from the play area's edge; the slack goes to the outer side, so what "
        .. "the player sees is the run's slack rather than EDGE_PAD itself -- and "
        .. "because the window is one size that is 8px for EVERY crop, where "
        .. "1.8.0's per-speaker panel made it 8, 6 or 10 depending on who was "
        .. "talking.  "
        .. "It used to be flush with that edge, which on a phone IS the edge of "
        .. "the screen.  The 16px of that border between the panel and the text "
        .. "pen is the whole of the gap, unchanged.",
      "FRAMED's panel is the GAME's window, and its size is a constant.  Every "
        .. "earlier release imitated the frame instead of asking for it.  1.4.0 "
        .. "and 1.6.0 used a fixed six-tile square and stretched the art into a "
        .. "window inside it -- a nine-pixel ring of flat white, 61% of the "
        .. "panel, measured by .probe/dp3_fill_probe.lua -- which cost the art "
        .. "its 1:1 pixels.  1.8.0 sized the panel to the art and painted a "
        .. "one-pixel black outline where a border should be, which removed the "
        .. "ring but made the panel's WIDTH a property of the portrait, so the "
        .. "text got 19, 21 or 22 columns depending on who was talking.  This "
        .. "release asks Chrome.stdFrame -- the same call the start menu and the "
        .. "OPTION page are drawn with -- for the engine's own 48px window around "
        .. "a 32px content rect, so the ring is a real tile-drawn border, the "
        .. "art is a whole number of times the crop, and the text width is a "
        .. "constant again: 152px for every speaker in this layout.  That is the "
        .. "trade -- a constant text width and an honest border, at the price of "
        .. "a window bigger than most crops need.",
      "A page never ends on a single word.  The engine's wrap is greedy and "
        .. "has no short-line balancing (text_ir.lua's wrap_subline); at "
        .. "vanilla's 208 that never shows, but at the 152 a portrait costs it "
        .. "does, and on Gen 3 a third line becomes a new page rather than a "
        .. "scroll -- an A press to read one word.  The mod wraps "
        .. "TextIR.toTextBox and REFLOWS its answer: the last word of the line "
        .. "above moves down to join a one-word page.  It is a reflow, not a "
        .. "re-wrap, so no word is added, dropped or reordered and the number "
        .. "of lines and page breaks is unchanged -- the engine counts lines to "
        .. "decide pages, so a reflow that changed a line count would move "
        .. "every page boundary in the box.  It is armed on the width, so a "
        .. "MARGIN or OFF box keeps the engine's own text byte for byte.",
      "A portrait is drawn only for the dialogue frame.  world.talk says a "
        .. "conversation started; it does not say the box on screen is part of "
        .. "one, so a box the engine opens with another frame kind -- "
        .. "setFrame('battle') for an evolution, setFrame('sign') for a sign -- "
        .. "is bare even with a conversation still on record.  The egg hatch is "
        .. "NOT an example of that guard: egg_hatch.lua sets frame 'dialogue', "
        .. "so the guard passes and the box is the field box.  It is bare "
        .. "because hatching is step-driven and world.stepped has already "
        .. "dropped the press record.",
      "A shared graphic is now resolved by WHERE it is standing, not only by "
        .. "what it is.  A graphic is a uniform: 26 ROCKER, the yellow-haired "
        .. "figure, is a Juggler in Fuchsia Gym, a Bird Keeper on Route 13 and "
        .. "a Rocker on Route 12, and 55 SCIENTIST is a Super Nerd on Route 8 "
        .. "and a Scientist in Silph Co.  art/map_art.lua records, for every "
        .. "map, the picture its own trainers resolve to -- 91 maps, 228 "
        .. "graphic-to-picture pairs, 11 of them splits where one graphic is "
        .. "worn by two classes on one map and the majority wins.  It is "
        .. "consulted BETWEEN the trainer's own id and the graphics table, and "
        .. "it has to sit there rather than above the id, because the two "
        .. "disagree for 17 of the cart's 432 trainer objects -- a Route 16 "
        .. "Biker standing among Hikers, a Kindle Road Cooltrainer among Black "
        .. "Belts -- and in each of those the cart named that man himself.  "
        .. "Measured honestly the route changes exactly ONE non-trainer in the "
        .. "whole game, and 5 of its 6 answers already agreed; it earns its "
        .. "place as the answer for a boot where the generated trainer table "
        .. "is absent.",
      "The graphics table gained a default for the two shared sprites that "
        .. "needed one -- the Scientist for 55 and the Aroma Lady for 28, the "
        .. "majority class of each -- because the fallback is what a player "
        .. "sees whenever the id route cannot answer, and 107 and 'nothing at "
        .. "all' were the reported symptoms.",
      "The mod's own trainer index is no longer memoised BEFORE the engine is "
        .. "asked for its pack.  The cart's trainer table is a GENERATED "
        .. "cache, so a first call that found it missing cached an EMPTY index "
        .. "for the rest of the session and the id route stayed dead even "
        .. "after the table appeared -- which is exactly how a Super Nerd ends "
        .. "up wearing the Scientist's 107 and a Juggler the Bird Keeper's "
        .. "104.  The empty index is not stored now, so the next call retries.",
      "Seel is framed on its FACE.  The first cut of this crop was measured on "
        .. "the wrong picture -- mon-87, DEWGONG, whose head does sit at the top "
        .. "left.  A species is shown its own front pic: SEEL's internal species "
        .. "id is 86, and Pokemon.frontPic(86) is byte-identical to "
        .. ".probe/_art/mon-86.png.  Seel's own sprite is drawn front-on with the "
        .. "face LOW -- muzzle bbox (18,42)-(34,51), tongue (20,47)-(27,52) -- so "
        .. "both the rule's own { 13, 5, 32 } and the wrong { 4, 4, 32 } framed "
        .. "the top lobes and left the whole face outside.  The window is now "
        .. "{ 12, 21, 32 }.",
    },
    known = {
      "The crop is a quad drawn straight from the extracted picture, not a "
        .. "copy of its pixels.  LÖVE removed Image:getData in 11.0 and this "
        .. "engine targets 11.5, so a source picture cannot hand its pixels back "
        .. "at runtime -- the engine itself never calls getData either.  A quad "
        .. "needs no readback, keeps the one resample and goes through the "
        .. "picture's own nearest-neighbour filter.",
      "Ships no ROM-derived art.  Every portrait is cut at runtime out of the "
        .. "battle art the engine extracted from the player's own ROM -- a "
        .. "64x64 trainer front pic or a 64x64 species front pic -- using a "
        .. "rectangle from art/crops.lua, which is keyed by the front-pic id "
        .. "(not the class: Brock and Misty are both class 84 but pictures 116 "
        .. "and 117, so a class-keyed table could not frame them differently).  "
        .. "The species key is not the display name either: it is the engine's "
        .. "own keyName fold, lowercased with the separators stripped, so "
        .. "NIDORAN(F) is nidoranf and MR. MIME is mrmime -- and the mod asks "
        .. "the engine's own dex for that fold rather than carrying a second "
        .. "copy of it, because four of the cart's species are spelled with a "
        .. "sign, an apostrophe or a space and two of the four SPEAK.  "
        .. "It also takes SPEAKER-keyed exceptions -- name:, gfx:, sprite: and "
        .. "class: prefixes, tried most specific first -- for the case a picture "
        .. "key cannot express: two speakers who share a picture and are not "
        .. "framed the same way.  A speaker key always outranks a picture key.  "
        .. "There is deliberately no species: prefix, because for a Pokemon the "
        .. "species IS the speaker.  A malformed entry is ignored rather than "
        .. "obeyed, so it falls through instead of drawing a one-pixel window.",
      "The Fisherman NPC's window is the DEFAULT, and that is a 1.9.2 result "
        .. "rather than an omission.  Picture 38 -- the Hoenn Fisherman -- is "
        .. "the SPARSEST of all 148 trainer pictures at 17% ink, because he is "
        .. "drawn seated bottom-right with his rod sweeping up-left so a centred "
        .. "square lands almost entirely on empty water, and 1.9.1 filed a "
        .. "hand-tuned window for him.  Nothing wears him any more: the class "
        .. "name FISHERMAN resolves to the Kanto class 69 rather than the Hoenn "
        .. "31, and picture 94 -- the fifteen BATTLE Fishermen -- is framed "
        .. "correctly by the default at 58%.  So 38's entry is retired along "
        .. "with the picture, and 94 is recorded in art/crops.lua as a "
        .. "measurement rather than as a rectangle that would only restate the "
        .. "default.  Worth reading once: it is what a wrong class name costs -- "
        .. "a measured, hand-tuned window filed against a picture that turns out "
        .. "to be unreachable.",
      "A name the cart spells with a sign, a quote or a space is read "
        .. "correctly.  The NAME: prefix token class is wider than it looks, "
        .. "because FireRed spells four of its 386 species with a character a "
        .. "tidier class rejects -- NIDORAN with the female and male signs "
        .. "(U+2640, U+2642), FARFETCH'D with an apostrophe, MR. MIME with a "
        .. "space -- and two of those four SPEAK, so before 1.8.2 both Nidoran "
        .. "resolved no speaker and drew no portrait.  The mod does not fold "
        .. "those names itself: it hands them to the engine's own norm_key, "
        .. "which already knows the sign means _F or _M.",
      "A class that covers several characters resolves to one of them -- all "
        .. "eight gym leaders share a class.  The graphics id is what tells "
        .. "those apart, so a leader standing in his own room gets his own "
        .. "face; the name route covers the cases where the dialogue names the "
        .. "speaker; CustomArt/ covers the rest.",
      "The default crop rule in art/crops.lua is one framing rule for "
        .. "everybody, plus 40 measured exceptions -- 9 trainer pictures and 31 "
        .. "species.  The species half is the world's Pokemon rather than only "
        .. "the ones that speak: 19 species have dialogue anywhere in the cart, "
        .. "and the world places 32 of the 42 Pokemon graphics ids, so the "
        .. "reachable total is 32 and 31 of them are filed.  (Voltorb is the one "
        .. "the default frames correctly -- a whole ball with both eyes in.)  "
        .. "The default window frames a whole creature's BODY, and most of these "
        .. "have artwork starting above it.  The table is still not a finished "
        .. "per-character one -- some faces sit off-centre until an override is "
        .. "added -- and the file's own header documents both key spaces (by "
        .. "picture, and by speaker) and when to reach for each.",
      "Some named characters get no portrait, on purpose -- the ones the cart "
        .. "never drew a picture of (the Nurse, the Clerk, Mom, Bill, the "
        .. "Chef, the Policeman) have no battle art in FRLG to cut a face out "
        .. "of, and cropping their overworld sprite would be a worse picture "
        .. "rather than a better fallback.  They are absent from SPRITE_ART "
        .. "rather than mapped to the nearest-looking class, because a wrong "
        .. "face is worse than no face.  A PNG dropped in CustomArt/ always "
        .. "wins and is the way to give them one.  The old folks are NOT on "
        .. "this list, though they used to be: the cart DID draw them, as the "
        .. "EXPERT pair (pictures 34 and 35), and between them they are the "
        .. "most common people in the game after the youngsters.",
      "The rival is recognised by the name on the player's save, so naming him "
        .. "something the trainer pack already knows (BROCK, say) gets the pack's "
        .. "answer rather than his own face.  The pack's name is tried first and "
        .. "wins outright, deliberately -- that is what keeps a script handing "
        .. "off between two characters correct.  Narrow in practice: the pack's "
        .. "429 names are mostly not things a player types for their rival.  His "
        .. "PICTURE is a constant rather than a lookup, because the cart spells "
        .. "two different rivals with that one class name: RIVAL_EARLY is class "
        .. "81 (picture 106) and RIVAL_LATE is 89 (picture 124), 89 carries the "
        .. "rows, so the name resolves to the LATE face -- a change nothing "
        .. "reported and 1.9.0 verified as 106.  The three routes that used to "
        .. "write 'RIVAL' write the number 106 instead (SPRITE_ART.SPRITE_BLUE, "
        .. "NAME_ART.RIVAL and the player's-own-name route), and CustomArt/"
        .. "RIVAL.png is the way to the other one.",
      "An ordinary NPC gets NO portrait rather than a shared one.  Two values "
        .. "in the cart mean 'none' -- class 0, which is what every non-trainer "
        .. "map object carries, and picture 0, the null picture the empty "
        .. "trainer record points at -- and neither is treated as a mapping.  "
        .. "0 is truthy in Lua, so an index that only asks 'is this a number?' "
        .. "hands picture 0 to every ordinary person in the game and they all "
        .. "wear the same face.",
      "MARGIN only has a margin to paint into when the window is wider than "
        .. "the 240x160 game frame, and only when that margin can hold the panel "
        .. "PLUS its clearance on both sides; where it cannot, the panel stands "
        .. "above the box instead, 2 game px clear of the box's top and 4 in "
        .. "from the play area's edge, and clamped so it never runs off the "
        .. "top of the frame.  It is never centred in the "
        .. "frame: the box lives in the bottom fifth of the screen, so a "
        .. "centred panel floats half a screen away from its own dialogue.",
      "The press record has three ends, not two: a step (world.stepped), a map "
        .. "change (map.entered), and the conversation's own script finishing "
        .. "(script.ended).  The third is not redundant -- a turn on the spot "
        .. "raises no world.stepped, because Player.tryMove sets the facing and "
        .. "returns 'turned' without ever reaching Player.finishStep -- and it "
        .. "deliberately survives a script that hands off to another with "
        .. "completed = false, since that is the same conversation continuing.",
      "Gen 3 is the engine's beta generation.  Written against release 0.3.0's "
        .. "src/ui/game3/* and src/core/game3/*.",
      "FireRed and LeafGreen only.  For Red/Blue/Yellow use "
        .. "gen1recomp-dialogue-portraits; for Gold/Silver/Crystal use "
        .. "gen2-dialogue-portraits.",
      "Tested to LOAD, not only to resolve.  tests/dp3_load_test.lua drives the "
        .. "engine's own headless Loader and asserts the mod is discovered, its "
        .. "body ran, and Message.show / Message.draw / FrlgFont.draw were "
        .. "replaced on the real modules with world.talk and render.hud linked -- "
        .. "then asserts the inverse on a Gen 2 boot, where the mod must install "
        .. "nothing.  The other suites drive exported resolvers, so on their "
        .. "own they would stay green if the mod never loaded at all.",
      "Reachable, not just installed.  FireRed has no route to the mod manager "
        .. "-- no F10 hotkey, no mods row anywhere in src/ui/game3/ -- so this "
        .. "mod does not push a foreign menu.  It puts its settings into "
        .. "FireRed's own OPTION menu, through the option menu's own "
        .. "row/group machinery (src/ui/game3/option_rows.lua), drawn by "
        .. "FireRed's own chrome and font: open the start menu, choose OPTION, "
        .. "and the last entry is DIALOGUE PORTRAITS.  Pushing the engine's "
        .. "ManagerState instead was tried and does not work here -- it renders "
        .. "with Gen 1 primitives and FireRed's extracted font has no glyphs "
        .. "for them, so it paints a blank screen.  "
        .. "tests/dp3_menu_test.lua walks the whole path and asserts the group "
        .. "is absent before the mod loads and gone once it is released.",
      "Per-speaker, not one-for-everybody.  tests/dp3_geometry_test.lua drives "
        .. "two different speakers through the real world.talk -> Message.show "
        .. "-> Message.draw path and asserts they PAINT two different pictures, "
        .. "and tests/dp3_speaker_test.lua asserts an ordinary NPC paints none. "
        .. "Both were added after a bug where every ordinary person in the game "
        .. "wore picture 0, and the suites were green because their art stub "
        .. "handed out a fresh image per call and could not tell one picture "
        .. "from another.",
    },
  },
  credits = {
    { who = "gen1recomp-dialogue-portraits and gen2-dialogue-portraits",
      for_ = "the idea, the three layouts and the speaker-resolution order" },
    { who = "pret/pokefirered",
      for_ = "the dialogue box geometry, the text printer semantics and the "
        .. "trainer class list this mod reads" },
    { who = "gen1recomp",
      for_ = "the Gen 3 field, UI and mod-loader stack" },
  },
  compat = { engine = ">=0.0.0-0 <2.0.0", modApi = 2 },
}
